-- int-tests-vintage-matrix: PLAN section 10, item 3. For each of the nine point-in-time texts of the Law and the day before each change, the three groups that answer a question about the text
-- (G1: "Minister", "Comptroller", sub-paragraph (ba); G7: the resolver and the same facts from the amending instruments; G9: the Dormant Bank Accounts words of Schedule 1) must agree with one another
-- and with the sources.  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Table of Legislation History (src:870-912) and the amending instruments, before the module was run:
--   * "Minister": Chief Minister in the text of 1 January 2019; Minister for External Relations from R&O.40/2019 (31 May 2019); Minister for External Relations and Financial Services from R&O.29/2021 (2 March 2021);
--     Chief Minister again from R&O.28/2023 (12 April 2023); Minister for External Relations from R&O.10/2024 (9.30 a.m., 27 February 2024); Chief Minister from R&O.102/2026 (2 October 2026).
--   * "Comptroller": the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961 until 31 December 2019; the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019 from 1 January 2020 (L.13/2019 Sch 3 para 1, R&O.136/2019).
--   * sub-paragraph (ba): inserted by R&O.56/2025, made 9 October 2025, in force 7 days after, so from 16 October 2025.
--   * the Dormant Bank Accounts words of Schedule 1 (L.1/2017): from 16 December 2019.

§ `Integration layer -- the vintage matrix`

GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
g7 MEANS `the favoured interpretation`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
g1 MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`an instant in Jersey` y mo d h mi s MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD y mo d) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mi s) "Europe/Jersey"

§§ `Each text of the Law: what the sources say, against what G1, G7 and G9 each answer`

GIVEN v IS A `Vintage of the text`
      minister IS AN `Office of the Minister`
      comptroller IS A `Law defining the Comptroller`
      ba IS A BOOLEAN
      dbal IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Text of the Law in force`
`the text as the sources give it` v minister comptroller ba dbal MEANS
    `Text of the Law in force` WITH
        vintage IS v
        `office of the Minister` IS minister
        `Law that the Comptroller is defined by` IS comptroller
        `paragraph (ba) is in Article 2(1)` IS ba
        `Schedule 1 carries the Dormant Bank Accounts words` IS dbal

#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 1 January 2019` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 1 January 2019` `the Chief Minister` `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 31 May 2019` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 31 May 2019` `the Minister for External Relations` `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 16 December 2019` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 16 December 2019` `the Minister for External Relations` `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 1 January 2020` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 1 January 2020` `the Minister for External Relations` `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 2 March 2021` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 2 March 2021` `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services` `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 12 April 2023` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 12 April 2023` `the Chief Minister` `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 27 February 2024` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 27 February 2024` `the Minister for External Relations` `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 16 October 2025` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 16 October 2025` `the Minister for External Relations` `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `the text of 2 October 2026` EQUALS `the text as the sources give it` `the text of 2 October 2026` `the Chief Minister` `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019` TRUE TRUE

-- Before the first consolidated text nothing is known: every part refuses, G1 and G9 and G7 alike.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` fleet `before the first consolidated version`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `before the first consolidated version`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `before the first consolidated version`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `before the first consolidated version`

§§ `G7 against G1: the Minister and the Comptroller, text by text (PLAN section 10, item 3)`

#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026`

-- The Comptroller: G7 names the enactment with its own type and G1 with another (nouns request 2 of G7: one should be kept); the two are the same fact when the constructors agree.
GIVEN a IS A `Law defining the Comptroller`
      b IS AN `Enactment that defines the Comptroller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
      WHEN `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961` THEN b EQUALS `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
      WHEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019` THEN b EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`

#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025`)
#ASSERT `the same Comptroller law in G1 and G7` (`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026`) (`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026`)

